### Which @angular/* package(s) are the source of the bug?

compiler

### Is this a regression?

Yes

### Description

```
@let value = 'one';

@if (true) {
  @let value = 1;
  {{ value }}
}
```

result:
![image](https://github.com/angular/angular/assets/8691013/21bb2a2a-46bd-4c31-926c-7d1eb2a942e1)
should be 1, not one.

app.component.js

![image](https://github.com/angular/angular/assets/8691013/426fada2-8094-4a93-b239-49229b5fcbff)

another problem
```
@let value = 'hello world';
<input #value (input)="0">
{{ value.value }}
```
will get a error

![image](https://github.com/angular/angular/assets/8691013/e5ab8c96-d0b2-4676-9fc7-465503e7509e)
looks like the value is not input ref, change the code to
```
@let value = 'hello world';
<input #value (input)="0">
{{ value }}
```
no more error, but the result is

![image](https://github.com/angular/angular/assets/8691013/6914f643-5426-45b5-8a0d-cf9a4fe4e10d)
it is a input ref...

![image](https://github.com/angular/angular/assets/8691013/0a92fe7b-883f-47c4-bb55-c0a0935a6eae)




